## Reflection (150–200 words)
While working on these tasks, I realized just how easy it is to fall into a scammer’s trap, even if you’ve never done anything that could compromise your security.
The scariest part came when I learned more about DNS—it’s unsettling to realize that a malicious actor could steal all my data simply by finding out which websites I visit.
I was also surprised to find that all the ports on my computer were open, which means I’m an easy target for a hacker.
I’ve started thinking much more seriously about my own online security—my studies in cybersecurity are already paying off.
It’s actually hard to say which commands I’d use most often, because they’re all needed at one time or another,
so I’d like to try to memorize most of them so that I can spend less time searching for the right commands as I continue working.
I really enjoyed exploring my computer and figuring out how hackers can steal user data.
